WEBVTT

00:00:00.386 --> 00:00:11.117
This is the web chat page BxAgents generates from one small gateway file. Here the server is protected, so the page asks for the password in a form, and remembers it.

00:00:11.816 --> 00:00:19.133
A new conversation opens with suggestions. One click sends it, and the answer streams in, here as a formatted list.

00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:27.257
When the agent calls a tool, you see a card with its status and a preview of the arguments. Open it to see exactly what was sent.

00:00:27.958 --> 00:00:33.462
Code comes back in a block with its language and a copy button, and the copy gives you the code itself.

00:01:02.756 --> 00:01:13.721
The header stays quiet. Everything else lives behind the settings gear: fork or export the conversation, your notes, appearance, the password, and for an admin, access tokens.

00:01:14.421 --> 00:01:22.506
Pick dark mode, and the choice follows your account. Notes are short facts the agent keeps about you. They are shared with the terminal chat.

00:01:23.206 --> 00:01:30.865
Admins can make named access tokens right here. The secret is shown once, so copy it now, and revoke any token later.
